BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:James Welling: Cento
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261213
DTSTAMP:20261104T182707Z
UID:7339357a303a56796091545c0b6c@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:This exhibition focuses on more than 60 recent works by photog
 rapher James Welling (American\, born 1951). From the artist’s Cento and
  Personae series\, these photographs of ancient sites in Italy and Greece
 \, as well as antiquities found in museums around the world\, were subject
 ed to digital and painterly alteration by the artist to achieve transforma
 tive effects. The photographs will be exhibited alongside a selection from
  the Museum’s extensive historic plaster cast collection of Greek and Ro
 man sculpture.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/james-welling-cento
LOCATION:Quick Center for the Arts\, Walsh Gallery\, 1073 N. Benson Road\,
  Bellarmine Hall - Art Museum\, Fairfield CT\, 06824-3826
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/james-welling-cento
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:We Live Here
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261219
DTSTAMP:20261104T182707Z
UID:561fc4d7ef1ba7afe9fe435470b7@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:An exhibition that looks at housing as the framework of commun
 ity life. With historical images\, photography\, architectural designs\, r
 esident testimony\, and interactive displays\, We Live Here will place a c
 entury of residential life in the greater New London area and Connecticut 
 in the broader context of the nation. The history of dwelling is our socia
 l history. It illuminates how our communities live now and could live bett
 er in the future.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/we-live-here
LOCATION:The Garde Gallery\, Garde Arts Center\, 305 State Street\, New Lo
 ndon CT\, 06320
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/we-live-here
END:VEVENT
